== Notes ==
* {{dlc|nr}} A possible encounter in [[Greed Mode#Greedier Mode|Greedier Mode]] may spawn up to 6 Sisters Vis.
* They can be found in {{s|The Void}}, even when not unlocked.

== Trivia ==
* Sisters Vis originated from the 2004 PC game ''[[wikipedia:Gish (video game)|Gish]]'', created by Edmund McMillen.
** In ''Gish'', they are the bosses of the 3rd area: '''The 7 Planes of Hehenna''', and went by the name "Vis Sisters" instead.
** As the Sisters Vis are originally from ''Gish''. The designs of the Vis enemies and The Cage itself originated from them.
* On the Sisters Vis' bodies, there is a Y-shaped mark. During an autopsy, an incision is made into the body and is stitched up afterward. The remaining Y-shaped mark is known as an autopsy stitch.
* Sisters Vis are the only normal boss that shoots the type of laser that is shot by {{e|Mega Satan}} and the item Mega Blast.
* There are [[Cut_Content#Sisters_Vis|unused]] textures for Sisters Vis in the base game (no DLC).
** The unlock condition for Sisters Vis would have been to "beat {{s|Sheol}} 10 times" and would have appeared in Sheol after being unlocked. It's unknown how this would work in-game, as {{e|Satan}} acts as one of the final bosses and always appears in Sheol.
* They appear to be wearing leather "gimp masks", which are attire used in BDSM.
** Another appearance of this mask in-game is from the item {{i|Gimpy}}.
** {{dlc+|r}} It is also worn by {{e|Whipper}}s and {{e|Snapper}}s while in {{s|Gehenna}}.{{dlc-}}

